NAME
    wmcalc - calculator WM client (Path C phase 32)

SYNOPSIS
    wmcalc [SECONDS]

DESCRIPTION
    Open a 220x320 calculator window.  SECONDS is the lifetime
    cap (default 600 = 10 minutes); Ctrl-Q exits early.

    Four-function integer calculator using two-register
    evaluation (pending op + accumulator).  Sequence "12 + 34 ="
    yields 46; chained ops fold left-to-right.

    Keys (delivered when the window has keyboard focus):
      0-9             digit
      + - * /         operator
      = or Enter      evaluate
      c or C          clear all
      Backspace       drop last digit of current entry
      _               toggle sign of current entry
      .               (no-op; integer-only build)
      Ctrl-Q          quit

    Mouse: click any button.  Buttons briefly highlight (one
    frame burst) when pressed.

    The pending operator is shown in the top-left of the display
    panel ('+', '-', '*', '/') while a chain is in progress.

LIMITATIONS
    Integer-only — libuser has no ftoa yet, so the '.' button is
    a placeholder.  Division truncates (e.g. 7 / 2 = 3).  Range:
    signed 64-bit, but digit entry caps at 11 digits to fit the
    display.  Division by zero shows "ERR" in red; clear with C.

SEE ALSO
    wmterm(1), wmedit(1), wmd(1)
